# 45. RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Use breakpoints approximately:

- Mobile: below 640px.
- Tablet: 640–1023px.
- Laptop: 1024–1279px.
- Desktop: 1280–1535px.
- Wide desktop: 1536px and above.

## Desktop

- Full sidebar.
- Flexible workspace.
- Resizable Live Workspace and inspectors.

## Laptop

- Compact or collapsible sidebar.
- Adjustable split views.
- Avoid forcing narrow unreadable columns.

## Tablet

- Collapsed navigation.
- Context panels become overlays or drawers.
- Keep main workspace readable.

## Mobile

Prioritize:

- AI Workspace.
- Task monitoring.
- Approvals.
- Notifications.
- Quick control.

Use compact bottom navigation or a navigation drawer.

Live Workspace becomes a separate screen or full-screen drawer.

Do not attempt to fit three desktop columns into a mobile viewport.

Touch targets should generally be at least 44px.

Avoid horizontal overflow except inside intentionally scrollable tables or canvases.

---

# 46. ACCESSIBILITY

Implement:

- Semantic HTML.
- Accessible labels.
- Visible keyboard focus.
- Keyboard navigation.
- Focus trapping in modal dialogs.
- Sufficient color contrast.
- Text alternatives for meaningful images.
- Accessible status labels.
- Reduced-motion support.
- Clear validation messages.

Do not rely on color alone to communicate task status.

Do not make important controls discoverable only through hover.

Use aria-live or appropriate accessible status announcements selectively for significant task changes.

Avoid announcing every progress event continuously.

